# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# go.work / go.work.sum are deliberately NOT ignored (memql#3165).
#
# Ignoring them contradicted the CI they have to work with: the `go` filter
# bucket in .github/workflows/ci.yml lists both files as lane inputs, so an
# ignored workspace file could never trigger the lane that exists to notice it.
# A workspace also changes what every `./...`-shaped selector resolves to
# across the whole repo -- exactly the kind of file that must be reviewed in a
# diff rather than living untracked on one machine and silently changing that
# machine's results. If the module split introduces one, it gets committed.

# Local repo-split staging area. Each subdirectory (.split/memql,
# .split/memql-cockpit, .split/<carrier-repo>) holds a candidate
# repo layout while the monorepo is being carved up. Never committed
# to the core repo; once a candidate is validated, it gets pushed to
# its own remote and the staging copy is discarded.
/.split/

# env file
.env
.env.local
.env.*
# Keep the checked-in template that documents the override schema.
!.env.example

# Cloud Run env reference file (contains secrets - do not commit)
cloud-run-env.yaml

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/
__debug*
bin/
/memql
/memql-service
/bridge-agent
# Stray output of `go build ./cmd/memql-cockpit`. Canonical build target is
# `make cockpit` -> bin/memql-cockpit; the headless and GUI variants both
# land under bin/. The dot-form `go build ./cmd/memql-cockpit` from the repo
# root drops the binary here, which has no business being tracked.
/memql-cockpit
/memql-cockpit-gui
# Stray output of `go build ./scripts/secrets` (the operator CLI). Normal flow
# uses `go run`, so this binary is always an accident. The file name is
# alarming -- ignore so it never gets staged.
/secrets

# local environment files
.env.*
!.env.example
*.local
.gocache/

# Exception: allow .claude/skills/*-local/ skill directories
!.claude/skills/*-local/

# Claude Code scratch state (not shared across machines)
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/worktrees/

# Temporary files and logs
temp/
logs/

# Node.js -- the TS SDK under sdk/ts/, the view-kit renderer under
# sdk/ts-viewkit/ and the portal under clients/portal/ are checked-in node
# consumers in this monorepo (memql#116, memql#3314). Their package.json is
# checked in; everything else stays ignored. The deploy/gate-browser
# Playwright gate is also checked in -- its lockfile is what pins the npm deps
# by integrity hash (Scorecard PinnedDependencies).
package.json
!sdk/ts/package.json
!sdk/ts-viewkit/package.json
!clients/portal/package.json
!deploy/gate-browser/package.json
package-lock.json
!sdk/ts/package-lock.json
!sdk/ts-viewkit/package-lock.json
# The portal is an APPLICATION, so its lockfile IS committed: it pins the exact
# dependency tree the released bundle is built from, which is what makes
# `npm ci` reproducible in CI and in the image build. sdk/ts is a library and
# deliberately has none -- a library's lockfile constrains nothing downstream.
!clients/portal/package-lock.json
!deploy/gate-browser/package-lock.json
node_modules/

# The portal's build output. Produced by `make portal-build` (vite) and copied
# into the image by the Dockerfile's portal stage. Never committed: keeping
# minified bundles and hashed filenames out of git is precisely why the Go side
# serves them from a directory instead of //go:embed'ing them (see
# component/portal/doc.go).
clients/portal/dist/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Tailwind output for the identity web app — regenerated by
# scripts/identity/build-css.sh; run as part of make identity
# and the Dockerfile build.
component/identity/web/static/app.css

# Tailwind standalone CLI cache (per-platform binary downloaded
# on demand by scripts/identity/build-css.sh).
bin/tools/

# Locally-generated TLS certs for the dev cluster. mkcert produces
# these via scripts/dev/setup-tls.sh; they're per-machine (signed
# by the developer's local mkcert root CA) and must never be
# committed.
docker/nginx/certs/*.crt
docker/nginx/certs/*.key

# Generated docs reference (produced by cmd/docs-gen at bundle/release time)
docs/public/reference/_generated/*
!docs/public/reference/_generated/.gitkeep
# Docs bundle staging + tarballs
/docs-bundle/
/docs-*.tgz
# local tool builds (go build ./cmd/<tool> drops the binary in cwd)
/memqlmigrate
/memqllint
/memqlfmt

# Agent stack -- local credentials and MCP config (never commit).
.mcp.json

# Subagent-driven-development scratch workspace (ledger, briefs, review packages)
.superpowers/
